        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(imessage): prevent duplicate messages after delayed sends",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where an iMessage send could complete through `imsg`'s AppleScript fallback after a private-bridge stall, while OpenClaw reported a timeout and prompted the caller to retry. Those retries could deliver duplicate messages.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe dedicated send timeout is increased from 150 seconds to 180 seconds. This lets the outer RPC outlive `imsg`'s 150-second bridge deadline plus its fallback verification window, while leaving the 10-second probe timeout unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers should receive one message instead of duplicates when the private iMessage bridge stalls but the fallback send succeeds.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- A single cron session produced persisted messages at 09:03:14, 09:05:57, and 09:06:19 after the first two 150-second RPC timeouts triggered retries.\n- Focused test: `pnpm exec vitest run extensions/imessage/src/send.test.ts` (52 passed).\n- `oxfmt --check` and `git diff --check` pass.\n- Codex autoreview: no findings; patch rated correct with 0.98 confidence.\n\nAI-assisted: diagnosis, implementation, test updates, and independent review were performed with Codex under maintainer supervision.\n",
